description:
Replicates the DHIS2 Climate Tools population-weighting guide server-side. Loads a climate dataset and a WorldPop population dataset, computes the population-weighted mean of the climate variable within each GeoJSON feature for each time step — sum(value * population) / sum(population) — and exports CHAP-ready wide CSV (one row per location-period).

The population is loaded without a temporal filter and averaged to a single weighting surface inside aggregate_spatial_weighted (its spatial pattern is stable year to year, and the weighted mean is normalised), then aligned to the climate grid by nearest-neighbour interpolation.

Usage — submit as a process graph (synchronous POST /result or a batch job):

{
  "agg": {
    "process_id": "aggregate_population_weighted_chap",
    "arguments": {
      "dataset_id": "cicero_pm25_daily",
      "population_dataset_id": "worldpop_population_1km_yearly",
      "temporal_extent": ["2023-01-01", "2023-01-31"],
      "geometries": { "type": "FeatureCollection", "features": [ ... ] },
      "period_type": "day"
    },
    "result": true
  }
}
